From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: ROG5 wake on charger attach

Plugging a charger or cable into a ROG5 suspended on battery did not resume
it: the ADSP's USB property notification arrives through the IRQF_NO_SUSPEND
glink interrupt during s2idle, but power_supply_changed() only registers a
soft wakeup event, which does not end s2idle. The sleep policy keeps the
phone awake on USB power, so it must resume to notice the charger.

With the ROG5 OEM client, make the battmgr device wakeup capable and raise
a hard wakeup event for USB property notifications. Battery notifications
do not wake the system.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c	2026-09-28 11:42:44.385616575 +0200
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c	2026-09-28 11:43:34.066651750 +0200
@@ -1709,6 +1709,15 @@
 		qcom_battmgr_asus_chg_kick(battmgr, false);
 		break;
 	case NOTIF_USB_PROPERTY:
+		/*
+		 * ROG5: a charger/cable attach must wake a suspended phone
+		 * (its sleep policy stays awake on USB power). This callback
+		 * runs from the IRQF_NO_SUSPEND glink interrupt during s2idle,
+		 * where the power supply core's soft wakeup event does not end
+		 * the suspend. While awake the event is harmless.
+		 */
+		if (battmgr->oem_client)
+			pm_wakeup_hard_event(battmgr->dev);
 		power_supply_changed(battmgr->usb_psy);
 		qcom_battmgr_asus_chg_kick(battmgr, false);
 		break;
@@ -2297,6 +2306,9 @@
 			return PTR_ERR(battmgr->oem_client);
 
 		psy_cfg.attr_grp = qcom_battmgr_asus_groups;
+		ret = devm_device_init_wakeup(dev);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
 
 		/* Charge control defaults: auto, 0-100 %, i.e. no limit */
 		mutex_init(&battmgr->asus_chg_lock);
